Game Stream for Ubuntu amd64
===========================

Install with:
  sudo apt install ./game-stream_0.2.7_amd64.deb

Open Applications > Game Stream. First launch requires internet and about 2 GB
of free disk space for its private Python dependencies and Chromium browser.
A progress dialog reports setup. Native system dependencies are installed by
apt; no Python packages or browsers are downloaded by root maintainer scripts.
The per-user runtime is under ~/.local/share/game-stream (or XDG_DATA_HOME).
If interrupted, launch again. A previous working runtime is kept if an update
fails. Setup diagnostics are in ~/.local/state/game-stream/setup.log.

Close the app before uninstalling. Run as the normal desktop user:
  game-stream-uninstall
Optional removal of this user's preferences/session/catalog/inactive debug captures:
  game-stream-uninstall --purge-user-data
Dry run:
  game-stream-uninstall --dry-run

Or remove only the system package:
  sudo apt remove game-stream
This preserves user runtime/settings; the uninstall helper removes the owned
runtime too. Never run the application itself with sudo.

Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/26.04 amd64 with Python 3.10-3.15 is the intended target.
Other desktop Linux distributions can use the documented source installation.
This is not an Android APK and does not run on Android.

Standalone uninstall tools are also distributed with each release:
  bash uninstall-game-stream.sh [--dry-run] [--purge-user-data]
The game-stream-uninstaller_0.2.7.tar.gz bundle contains this script and instructions.

Release 0.2.7 fixes premature handoff after incidental HLS requests: it waits for
playing video, skips finite/VOD page fallbacks, keeps Chromium alive with refreshed
cookies and permits a later switch to the fragment bridge. Duplicate chunks are
skipped without permanently disabling that player's forwarding. Initial VLC
failures are reported as a player startup failure, not an ended broadcast.
Diagnostics include per-pane VLC state, relay type and browser segment counters.

Quadrant-number settings include offsets, opacity and independent always-on or
timed fading. Preferences > Quadrant numbers selects visibility, corner, size,
horizontal/vertical insets, opacity and the idle delay before fading. Numbers
retain their original quadrant IDs across zoom/layout changes. No video frame
copies or new browsers are needed.
Preferences > Diagnostics enables startup resource captures and offers a restart
with session restoration. Each launch creates a fresh timestamped folder under
~/.local/state/game-stream/debug (or XDG_STATE_HOME). A separate sampler writes
bounded resource logs even if the UI stalls; UI heartbeats record responsiveness.
Open the debug folder, start a fresh capture, or clear saved captures from this
tab. ZIP the relevant capture folder with load/stall/stop times for debugging.
Captures contain per-process memory/CPU/threads/descriptors, system RAM/swap
pressure and approved settings; no command lines, URLs, cookies, session file or
raw memory dumps. The manual monitor-resources.py remains available as well.
Default source quality remains 720p; the underlying buffer/relay limits from
0.2.4 are unchanged. Resource diagnostics are measurement, not an assumed fix for
all Chromium/GPU/native VLC behavior on a particular host.
Update checks are under Preferences > Updates; private repository access uses
the normal user's existing GitHub CLI login. Download failures keep playback.
